        "content": {
          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "To find Canadian downloadable digital directories, consider the following sources:\n\n### **1. Canadian Business Directories**\n- **Scott’s Directories**: Offers downloadable business directories for Canadian companies across industries. [Visit Scott’s Directories](https://www.scottsdirectories.com).\n- **InfoCanada**: Provides access to detailed Canadian business information. You can export data in various formats. [Visit InfoCanada](https://www.infocanada.ca).\n\n### **2. Public and Government Databases**\n- **Canada Business Network**: Lists government and business directories. Some are downloadable. [Visit Canada Business Network](https://www.canada.ca/en/services/business.html).\n- **Statistics Canada**: Provides open data directories and digital information. [Visit Statistics Canada](https://www.statcan.gc.ca).\n\n### **3. Industry-Specific Directories**\n- **Chamber of Commerce Listings**: Many Canadian Chambers of Commerce offer local business directories for download.\n- **Yellow Pages Canada**: Some areas allow downloadable versions of their directories. [Visit Yellow Pages](https://www.yellowpages.ca).\n\n### **4. Online Marketplaces**\n- **Etsy** and **Amazon**: Sometimes, digital versions of Canadian business directories are sold here.\n\n### **5. Libraries and Universities**\n- Check with **Library and Archives Canada** or local public libraries, which often provide access to free or paid directories for download.\n\nIf you're looking for a specific type of directory (e.g., businesses, professionals, nonprofits), let me know, and I can refine the suggestions."
          ]
        },
